spider-man his great comic book covers  for nearly 70 years and the friendly  neighborhood hero has shown up in  countless video games since the early  80s  he's appeared in the Marvel vs. Capcom  in Lego series but he's also starred in  his own games on so many platforms from  the Atari 2600 to the ps4 but with  dozens of web slinging adventures out  there which ones are really worth your  time we looked at the last 30 plus years  of video game history to pick out the  eight best spider-man games you know  eight because like spiders have eight  legs and well anyway we limited the list  two games strictly starring Spidey and  we're gonna present them chronologically  there's no ranking here first up we're  going all the way back to 1991  spider-man the video game is a coin-op  arcade machine that mixed beat'em up and  platforming it was far from Spidey's  first game but this one gets bonus  points for offering two different styles  of gameplay and the game transitions  between radically zoomed in and out  cameras to show the action while  fighting or highlight the rest of the  city while exploring now we'll jump  ahead to 2000 when the simply titled  spider-man launched on ps1 and n64 those  platforms assured in the era of 3d  console games and Spidey was there to  crawl on walls swing from buildings and  beat up bad guys in a whole new  dimension it was a treat to see classic  villains like scorpion and Doc Ock in a  totally new way and each stage is  presented in a classic comic-book style  with appropriate fonts for dialogue and  loading screens that display comic book  cover art Sam Raimi spider-man trilogy  was a smash hit in the early aunts and  both Tobey Maguire and Willem Dafoe  added their voices to the first licensed  video game this adaptation from Treyarch  stands out for not just letting me play  through the events of the movie but for  incorporating a bunch of new scenes and  villains who didn't show up on the big  screen the icing on the cake here is a  bonus mode that lets you play any level  as the green goblin in an alternate  timeline where a different more evil  goblin has been hired by Oscorp and if  we're gonna talk about games based on  movies we have to talk about spider-man  2 for the first time you could freely  move around the city exploring all of  Manhattan Plus Ellis Roosevelt and  Liberty Islands  for a long long time spider-man 2 was  the model for Spidey's movement using  physics to determine the path of his web  swings the open world was full of side  quests to complete to letting you rank  up your hero level to continue the main  story trailer took a step away from the  movies to put its own spin on ultimate  spider-man the first time a Spidey game  broke from the regular Marvel Comics  line like spider-man 2 this game let you  freely explore Manhattan and Peter  Parker's home borough of Queens but the  biggest difference is that you don't  just play as Spidey the plot is split  between spider-man and venom who has a  much more brutal combat style and not  just because he has to eat people to  stay alive both characters have their  own plots and side quests that weave  together in a story involving Peter  Parker and Eddie Brock's parents if  playing is both good and evil characters  an ultimate spider-man sounds cool then  you'll love what web of Shadows brings  to the table this game focused on the  internal clash between Spidey and the  symbiote letting you switch between the  red and black suits at any time each  with their own powers but it's not just  about what spider-man looks like  throughout the game you can choose  between good or evil actions and even  which villains you want to fight web of  Shadows has multiple endings based on  your decisions changing which female  companion Spidey ends up with and even  determining whether or not he ends the  game as an actual good guy that cause  and effect goes even further in  spider-man edge of time this game also  features two heroes jumping between the  regular webhead and spider-man 2099 each  with their own abilities and skill trees  each hero is actually trapped in the  other's timeline in actions taken by  spider-man 2099 in the past actually  alter the future for the other  spider-man there's definitely a lesson  here about messing with time travel and  finally we have to talk about the most  recent Spidey game Marvel's spider-man  comes from insomniac the team that  brought us Ratchet and Clank and sunset  overdrive games that emphasize creative  use of gadgets and freedom of movement  insomniacs take on spider-man just feels  good whether you're slinging webs or  swinging punches at bad guys the  original story is packed with great  moments but if you just want to explore  the city there are plenty of side quests  and optional objectives to extend your  stay in New York  and it's definitely the standard for  Spidey games from here on out so those  are our picks for the best spider-man  games if you've got a favorite that  didn't make the list let us know in the  comments and for an even deeper look  back at Spidey's past you can always  check out our video on the history of  spider-man games  [Music]
 

